    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and working. Here's what was fixed:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Bug:** `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file. The `--ci` flag was being consumed at the global level and not passed to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Root Cause:** Commander.js was parsing known global options (`--ci`) before delegating to subcommands, preventing the flag from reaching the gate command handler.\n\n**Solution:** Three changes to `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:\n\n1. Added `.enablePositionalOptions(true)` to the main program (line 604) to allow positional options to pass through\n2. Added `.passThroughOptions(true)` to the `gate` command (line 742) to explicitly pass through all options\n3. Changed the action handler to extract raw arguments directly from `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)` instead of relying on Commander.js's parsed args. This bypasses the parser and ensures `--ci` and other flags reach the frai-gate CLI intact.\n\n**Verification:** Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build` and tested `frai gate init --ci` successfully creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
